    "body": "Toyota is recalling 19,000 electric C-HR SUVs globally, with about 10,000 affected in the US.\nToyota C-HR EV recall expands globally\nIn September, Toyota issued a safety recall involving certain model-year 2026 C-HR electric SUVs in North America.\nToyota initially said about 10,000 models were involved, but later confirmed the number was 8,521 in a letter to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA).\nAccording to Germany’s federal motor authority, Kraftfahrt-Bundesamt (KBA), the recall has now expanded to 19,000 C-HR vehicles globally. In Germany, the recall impacts 1,096 vehicles and is still under investigation by the KBA.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nThe issue stems from faulty software programming in the EV-ECU. While it’s intended to limit the battery’s charge level, the software can cause it to overcharge under certain conditions.\nToyota said the issue occurs if the battery is already at a high state of charge and the driver continues using the regenerative braking system.\nWhen this happens, warning lights and a sound will alert the driver, and the electric drive system can shut down, causing the vehicle to lose power while driving.\nToyota C-HR EV (Source: Toyota)\nFollowing an internal investigation, Toyota said in the NHTSA report that the issue was caused by incorrect software that disrupted the charging-limit function, allowing the battery to overcharge while driving.\nThe Toyota C-HR vehicles included in the recall were produced between June 17, 2025, and July 9, 2026.\nIn Europe and other overseas markets, Toyota sells the C-HR EV as the C-HR+ to distinguish it from the gas- or hybrid-powered version.\nToyota C-HR XSE interior (Source: Toyota)\nOwners of affected vehicles in North America can take them to a Toyota dealership, where the battery ECU software will be updated free of charge.\nToyota mailed owner notification letters out on October 18, 2026. Owners can contact Toyota’s customer service at 1-800-331-4331. The recall number is 26TA17.\nOther than saying the EV-ECU is being reprogrammed, Toyota has not yet announced next steps for owners of affected vehicles outside North America. The KBA reference number is 17116R.\nCheck back for more details. The recall only affects the 2026 C-HR. The 2027 Toyota C-HR is also now on sale.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
